<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The mood consequence of the TakeUpArms edict (EdictDefs/Edicts_Combat.xml, system 9: AI — combat). Its own
    file rather than an addition to Thoughts_Edicts.xml, for the reason CLAUDE.md gives: the loader reads
    every file under this directory, and a new file cannot conflict with another lane mid-edit on the shared
    one. Same situational ThoughtWorker_UnderEdict shape as the five there, so it appears and disappears
    exactly with GodManager.Activate/Deactivate and leaves nothing behind.

    Steeper than any of them (-3 to -4 there, scaled by how much routine work an edict displaces) because
    this one does not displace work at all — it asks people to go and meet an armed enemy with whatever is in
    their hands.
  -->

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>UnderTakeUpArms</defName>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.God.ThoughtWorker_UnderEdict</workerClass>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>called to arms</label>
        <description>We are all soldiers now, whether we have a weapon or not.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-6</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
